   221	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   222	    """
   223	    Reconstruct a hidden full diagonal between same-color endpoints, render it as a dashed line, then emit perpendicular rays from offset trigger pixels adjacent to that hidden path.
   224	
   225	    Input structure:
   226	    - The background is the dominant color. One non-background color appears as endpoint pairs on shared 45-degree diagonals, while trigger pixels of another color sit one perpendicular-diagonal step beside interior cells of those diagonals rather than directly on them.
   227	
   228	    Rule:
   229	    - For each maximal diagonal endpoint pair, infer the full endpoint-to-endpoint path but only paint every other path cell in the line color, producing a dashed connector.
   230	    - For every non-line pixel found one perpendicular-diagonal step away from any interior hidden-path cell, extend that pixel's color along the path's perpendicular diagonal in both directions, starting from the trigger pixel itself and filling only background cells.
   231	
   232	    Key insight:
   233	    - The visible blue cells are only a sampled trace of the real path. Triggers are validated against the invisible complete diagonal, so a magenta pixel can activate even when it sits beside a blank gap in the dash pattern.
   234	    """
